 "notes": "Controller: IK-based (damped least squares with nullspace pull to home pose) keeping the hand palm-down; yaw of the hand is chosen among cube-face-aligned candidates (plus small offsets) by an offline kinematic dry-run in __init__ (reachability, torso/self-contact check, joint motion cost; shoulder roll capped at 0.0 rad to avoid torso collisions). Sequence: joint-space move to above-pick pose, descend (site offset 2 cm toward thumb side and +0.8 cm up from cube centre \u2014 empirically tuned), close hand gradually, lift, translate and rotate wrist to the destination (compensating the measured cube-in-hand offset using observed cube and grasp-site positions), descend onto the destination cube, open, retreat. A lag guard stalls the Cartesian goal if the arm doesn't track. Measured about 90-95% success on practice seeds. Known weaknesses: destination or pick cubes very close to the torso (x\u22480.17, y\u2248-0.11..-0.14) sometimes have no feasible plan (arm collides with torso / IK stalls -> timeout), and the arm swinging near such cubes can knock them off the table. Planning uses the task's initial block poses (exact); runtime uses observed poses, so large sensing bias could hurt grasp alignment.",
